prompt:
14 seconds, 16:9. ONE LOCKED SHOT, NO CUTS. A wide shot from behind and above THE MOUNT; the camera never moves.

THE MOUNTAIN RISES. Ahead of them, where no land can be, a mountain comes up out of the flat sea while they are busy fishing.

REFERENCES, each with a job:
@Image 1: THE MOUNTAIN. Take its shape, its size in the frame and its darkness exactly.
@Image 2: THE CREATURE. Take its look exactly.
@Image 3: THE STRONG ONE. Face, body and colours only; take nothing of the white background.
@Image 4: THE YOUNG ONE. Face, body and colours only; take nothing of the white background.
@Image 5: THE ELDER. Face, body and colours only; take nothing of the white background.
@Image 6: THE TURNING LIGHT. A colour reference only: the deep indigo of the water inside the child's circle of light; nothing of its sky, its light or its composition.

THE FRAME: Wide from behind and above: THE MOUNT small in the lower third on flat black water in the rain, lit only by THE YOUNG ONE; the far black water ahead of it fills the upper frame.

STATE: THE MOUNT, the manta-like creature with its driftwood seat and bone-rib backrest; nothing on it gives off any light. Their skin, the seat and the back of THE MOUNT are wet and glistening with rain.

THE LIGHT: Once THE YOUNG ONE is glowing, the only light in the whole frame comes from the child: a warm golden glow from the child's whole body, gill frills blazing gold. It lights a circle exactly 2 metres in radius around the child and nothing beyond it. Inside the circle the black water turns to the deep indigo water of the turning, and the riders and THE MOUNT are lit gold; outside the circle everything is pitch black. Nothing else in the frame gives off light. Far beyond the circle the rising mountain is only a vast blacker shape against the dark; its two eyes, when they open, glow pale yellow-green on their own, the only other light in this shot.

WHAT HAPPENS:
[0s] THE YOUNG ONE glows warm gold from the whole body, lighting the circle of water 2 metres around the child, indigo inside, pitch black outside. All three are busy fishing: THE STRONG ONE lies across the front grabbing at fish with both arms in the water; THE YOUNG ONE kicks both feet in the water, giggling; THE ELDER rinses their one fish.
[3s] Far ahead the flat sea bulges and a vast dark shape rises like a mountain until it fills the upper half of the frame. THE ELDER stops and stares at it; the other two keep fishing.
[7s] THE YOUNG ONE notices THE ELDER staring, follows the gaze, goes still, then shakes THE STRONG ONE's shoulder; THE STRONG ONE looks up.
[10s] High on the mountain two enormous pale yellow-green eyes with thin slit pupils open, each bigger than their village, looking down at them. THE STRONG ONE's hands stop in the water.

Sound: only the sounds the characters make themselves: splashing hands and feet and THE YOUNG ONE's giggle, then THE YOUNG ONE's sharp gasp, then total silence as the eyes open; no words. No music, no ambient sound.

Colour grade, the dark with the child's light: pitch-black water in steady rain, the warm golden glow of THE YOUNG ONE the only light, deep indigo water inside its 2-metre circle, deep true blacks everywhere else.

Avoid: no words spoken by anyone, no talking, no shouted words, no voiceover, no roar, no teeth, no third eye, no camera move, no waves, no eyes before the last beat.
